# COMMAND — STANDING SPEC

Command is Sawyer's Claude Cowork project and the product brain for this repo.
This file loads on every request. Sawyer does not relay messages between us.

The GitHub Actions `@claude` bot is NOT Command. It has no memory and no design record. Do not route product decisions through it.

## READ BEFORE YOU BUILD

These are the spec. Read them, do not summarize them away:

- `design/COMMAND-BRAIN.md` — product model, surfaces, visual system, language
- `design/LISTING-ENGINE.md` — **the backbone.** Identify, titles, descriptions, channels, templates, pricing
- `design/BASE44-TRUTH.md` — what Base44 got right, what it got wrong, real screen names
- `design/CURSOR-BUILD-ORDER.md` — ordered workstreams

## NON-NEGOTIABLES

1. **Do not reskin the same broken shell in a new color.** Three palettes have been shipped over a non-functional app. That is not progress and it will be rejected again.
2. **Do not invent tab names.** "Rail" is not Sawyer's word — it appeared in the current build and he never approved it. Real names are in `BASE44-TRUTH.md`. If a surface has no name there, ask.
3. **Do not ship identify as barcode-only.** Barcode covers sealed product with a UPC. It covers almost none of what he sells. See the IDENTIFY section of `LISTING-ENGINE.md`.
4. **Do not build without the engine spec.** The listing engine is the AI core. Without it nothing downstream can be correct.
5. **Ask one question if a provider or API-key decision is required. Do not pick alone.** Ask Sawyer, then stop and wait.
6. **Verify before claiming done.** Click it in a running build. If you did not verify, say so explicitly.
7. **One repo.** This one.

## CURRENT STATE — verified live on https://f-o-b.vercel.app

- **Identify is dead.** Photos drop fine. Clicking identify fires **zero network requests** and spins forever. There is no backend behind it.
- **Inventory is not built.** Near-blank page, info stacked at top.
- **Only the photo dump works.** Everything else is chrome over nothing.

Behavior outranks visuals. Do not touch the palette until identify and inventory function.

## VISUAL — hard rules

- **Banned:** `#F5C518`, school-bus/Crayola yellow, gold-on-black form chrome, gold buttons, gold gradients. Rejected three times.
- **Banned:** green as a primary or accent color. Bright/neon green especially — it hurts his eyes. Green-black has failed in past builds.
- Accent: restrained amber `#F2A03D` on near-black `#07080A`. Panels `#0E1113`. Raised `#151A1D`.
- Accent covers **under 10% of screen area** — hairlines, one active state, small glyphs. Never large fills.
- Dark teal `#2E6B6E` is structural only — rails, connectors, inactive nodes. Not a second accent.
- Type: **Orbitron** for chrome only (uppercase, letterspaced, ≤3 words). **Rajdhani** for everything else. Orbitron inside a sentence reads amateur.
- Materials: 1px hairline + `backdrop-filter: blur(14px)`; glow via `box-shadow` at 8–12% opacity, never text-shadow bloom; 2–3% noise overlay.
- Motion: 180–240ms, `cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1)`. Nothing snaps.
- **Every space and tab needs an obvious way to back out.**
- Avoid the desaturated "blue colored pencil" look.
- Bar: Sawyer's taste is level 100. Base44 hit ~50. The reskins landed below that.

## LANGUAGE

Plain English in all UI. **Banned words:** deploy, archive, purge, supply, rail. Use Add, Saved, Delete, Stock, Staged.
This is a reseller tool, not a collection manager.

## HOW TO TALK TO COMMAND — read this before you ever say "blocked"

Command replies on the GitHub issue. **Nothing pings you when a reply lands.** There is no push channel from Command to Cursor. If you wait to be notified, you will wait forever and Sawyer will find you idle.

**Before you say "I never heard back" or "I don't know what to do":**

1. Re-read the **entire** issue thread, newest comment to oldest. Command's replies are posted as `CornDogSmugglerIND`.
2. Re-read this file and `design/LISTING-ENGINE.md`.
3. Only then may you say you're blocked — and you must name **the exact comment ID you read last**. "I'm blocked" with no comment ID is not a valid status.

**Command's replies are the ones written as spec** — headers, tables, explicit STOP/GO. The GitHub Actions `@claude` bot is not Command; its comments are code-grep output, not decisions.

**When you need something from Command:** post the question on the issue, state clearly that you are waiting, and stop. Do not build past it. Do not pick a provider yourself.

**When Command has answered:** say what you read, then do it. Never re-ask a question already answered in the thread.
